# CQ-11 · spatial-contradiction
#
# Question: Does any single document assert two different RCC-8 relations of the
#           same ordered figure/ground pair?
# Persona:  P2 — scene-data annotator / ML researcher. RCC-8's eight relations
#           are jointly exhaustive and pairwise disjoint, so two of them over
#           one pair is a contradiction — and nothing in the schema can see it.
# Spec:     docs/vson.md §5.7 (JEPD holds in the intended interpretation, not as
#           an axiom); §2.1 (internal consistency); §5.12
# Form:     ASK — a clean corpus answers false
# Note:     This is a defect SHACL structurally cannot catch: each fact is its
#           own node carrying its own single `vso:rcc`, so every shape passes
#           while the pair of facts says two incompatible things. No OWL rule
#           reports it either — `ontology/rcc8.ttl` ships the eight as a closed
#           value vocabulary and asserts no composition table (§5.7). A query is
#           the mechanism that reaches it, which is one reason this pack exists.
PREFIX vso: <https://w3id.org/vson/v1/ontology#>

ASK {
  GRAPH ?doc {
    ?first  a vso:SpatialFact ;
            vso:figure ?figure ; vso:ground ?ground ; vso:rcc ?one .
    ?second a vso:SpatialFact ;
            vso:figure ?figure ; vso:ground ?ground ; vso:rcc ?other .
    FILTER(?one != ?other)
  }
}
